 { q: 'Are electricians in Nevada required to wear FR clothing?', a: 'Not in every task. Nevada OSHA enforces OSHA electrical rules that require the employer to assess flame and arc hazards. When an electrician is exposed to an arc with estimated incident energy above 2.0 cal/cm², arc-rated clothing with a rating at least equal to that estimate is required under 29 CFR 1910.269 and 1926.960.' },
